WEBVTT

00:00.300 --> 00:01.490
Buying a new Mercury?

00:02.160 --> 00:05.570
Get the shaft length wrong
and it never runs right.

00:06.140 --> 00:08.310
Checking it takes 5 minutes.

00:09.781 --> 00:13.131
Shaft length sets where
the prop sits in the water.

00:13.781 --> 00:15.851
The flat plate just above the prop

00:15.941 --> 00:18.591
should ride about level
with the bottom of the hull.

00:20.072 --> 00:22.372
Too short, and the prop pulls air

00:22.392 --> 00:25.342
and the revs spike under load.

00:25.872 --> 00:30.522
Too long, and the lower unit
drags, costing you speed and fuel.

00:32.113 --> 00:35.443
With the boat level, measure
from the top of the transom,

00:35.633 --> 00:39.903
where the motor mounts, straight down
to the bottom of the hull at the centre.

00:41.359 --> 00:43.599
About 15 inches is a short shaft.

00:43.619 --> 00:46.629
20 is a long shaft,

00:46.819 --> 00:48.379
the L in the model name.

00:48.399 --> 00:52.149
25 is extra long, XL.

00:53.539 --> 00:56.389
Most aluminum fishing boats
around here take a 20.

00:57.867 --> 01:01.117
Don't trust the old motor,
it may have been wrong too.

01:02.007 --> 01:04.257
A setback bracket changes the answer.

01:05.027 --> 01:07.877
And if you land between
sizes, don't round.

01:08.647 --> 01:10.537
Have your installer confirm it.

01:11.736 --> 01:15.546
On every repower, we measure
the transom before we order.

01:16.296 --> 01:19.486
Build your quote at mercuryrepower.ca.
